<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding the time a ball will reach at a given height</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A ball is thrown vertically upwards from the top of a platform \({@h0@}\ \mathrm{m}\) high. Its height \(h\) metres above the ground after \(t\) seconds is \[ h = {@hexpr@}. \]</p>
<p>At what times is the ball \({@HH@}\ \mathrm{m}\) above the ground? Give both times in the form \([a, b]\).</p>
<div>\(t = \) [[input:ans1]] seconds [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Set the height equal to \({@HH@}\) and rearrange into a <strong>quadratic equation</strong> equal to zero:</p>
\[ \begin{align*} {@hexpr@} &= {@HH@}\\ {@quad5@} &= 0\\ {@quad1@} &= 0 &&\text{divide by } 5\\ {@(t-t1)*(t-t2)@} &= 0. \end{align*} \]
<p>So \(t = {@t1@}\) or \(t = {@t2@}\). Both answers make sense: the ball passes \({@HH@}\ \mathrm{m}\) on the way up after {@t1@} seconds, and again on the way down after {@t2@} seconds.</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Graph of the height h against time t, with a horizontal line at h = {#HH#} crossing the curve at t = {#t1#} and t = {#t2#}.">
[[jsxgraph width="360px" height="300px"]]
(function() {
  var h0 = {#h0#}, v = {#vv#}, H = {#HH#}, t1 = {#t1#}, t2 = {#t2#}, hm = {#float(hmax)#};
  var tend = (v + Math.sqrt(v*v + 20*h0))/10;
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-0.6, hm*1.15, tend + 0.6, -hm*0.1], axis:true, grid:false,
      showNavigation:false, showCopyright:false});
  b.create('functiongraph', [function(t){ return h0 + v*t - 5*t*t; }, 0, tend], {strokeColor:'#1f5fa8', strokeWidth:2});
  b.create('line', [[0, H], [1, H]], {straightFirst:false, strokeColor:'#e67e22', dash:2, fixed:true});
  b.create('point', [t1, H], {name:'t = '+t1, size:4, fixed:true, color:'#c0392b', label:{offset:[-40,12]}});
  b.create('point', [t2, H], {name:'t = '+t2, size:4, fixed:true, color:'#c0392b', label:{offset:[6,12]}});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026063000</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>t1 : rand(3)+1;                    /* first time, 1..3 s */
t2 : t1+rand(3)+1;                 /* later time */
vv : 5*(t1+t2);                    /* initial speed, m/s */
h0 : rand(8)+3;                    /* platform height 3..10 m */
HH : h0+5*t1*t2;                   /* target height */
hexpr : h0+vv*t-5*t^2;
ts : [t1, t2];
quad5 : expand(5*(t-t1)*(t-t2));   /* 5t^2 - vt + (H - h0) */
quad1 : expand((t-t1)*(t-t2));
tmax : (t1+t2)/2;
hmax : ev(hexpr, t=tmax);
/* Misconceptions */
ts_neg : [-t1, -t2];
ts_one : [t1];
ts_wrong : [t1, t2+1];
/* Order-free version for marking: students may give the two times in either order. */
tset : setify(ts);</text>
    </questionvariables>
    <specificfeedback format="html">
      <text/>
    </specificfeedback>
    <questionnote format="html">
      <text>\(h = {@hexpr@}\), \(h = {@HH@}\) when \(t \in {@ts@}\)</text>
    </questionnote>
    <questiondescription format="html">
